//   D.1: Dependent/independent variables (+3, IDs exp-1 to exp-3)
//   D.2: Internal/external validity (+2, IDs exp-4 to exp-5)
//   D.3: Features of single-case designs (+2, IDs exp-6 to exp-7)
//   D.4: Advantages of single-case designs (+3, IDs exp-8 to exp-10)
//   D.5: Using single-case designs (+3, IDs exp-11 to exp-13)
//   D.6: Visual analysis rationale (+2, IDs exp-14 to exp-15)
//   D.7: Interpreting graphed data (+5, IDs exp-16 to exp-20)
// Answer distribution: A=5, B=5, C=5, D=5 (perfectly balanced)
